# Cgroup-escape sudoers rule for the isolated `/vibepro` development runner.
#
# Background: `systemctl restart openryoko` sends SIGKILL/SIGTERM to the
# whole service cgroup (KillMode=mixed in openryoko.service). Because the
# gateway starts the runner through `sudo -u ryoko-dev`, the runner used to
# live in that same cgroup and got killed mid-run by a routine restart,
# stranding the fail-closed development lock (observed 2026-07-31). This
# rule instead lets the gateway hand the runner to `systemd-run --scope`,
# which puts it in its own transient scope outside openryoko.service's
# cgroup — a gateway restart no longer touches it.
#
# Deploy: copy this file to /etc/sudoers.d/openryoko-development-scope
# (mode 0440, owned by root:root) and validate with `visudo -cf`. It
# REPLACES the older `(ryoko-dev)` direct-invocation rule documented in
# scripts/development-runner/README.md's "Gateway config" section — do not
# keep both rules active for the same runner path.
#
# Design note (fixed argv, no wrapper needed): this command line is
# intentionally 100% static — in particular it does NOT pass `--unit=...`.
# `systemd-run` auto-generates a unique transient unit name when `--unit` is
# omitted, so there is no per-invocation variable that would force either a
# wildcard sudoers rule (which would let the gateway's `ryoko` user run
# systemd-run with attacker-influenced arguments) or a root-owned wrapper
# script. sudo's exact-string match on the full argv is safe as-is. Add a
# wrapper script only if the invocation ever needs a genuinely per-run
# argument (e.g. embedding the Story id into `--unit=` for operator
# observability) — do not silently switch to a `*` wildcard to work around
# that need.
#
# The gateway-side config that must match this exact command is documented
# in scripts/development-runner/README.md under "Surviving gateway
# restarts" — keep both in lockstep when editing either one.

ryoko ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemd-run --quiet --collect --scope --uid=ryoko-dev --gid=ryoko-dev --setenv=HOME=/home/ryoko-dev /usr/local/libexec/openryoko-development-runner
